WHAT IT DOES. Two independent changes to the same sealed source, carried in one
patch because they cannot land separately: each would move the blob sha the
other's pin was measured over.

(A) THE LEASE HAND-DOWN (HERACLES-LEASE). Threads the wave's already-issued
python.offload Effect Lease through the GATED WRITE path, which is the path the
live loop actually takes:

  build_exec.WaveExecutor.run_wave  (lease acquired here, already landed)
    -> gated_writes.run_write_wave          <- needs the two new kwargs
      -> gated_writes.gate_candidates        <- needs them
        -> gated_writes._attempt_assignment  <- puts them in runner_kwargs
          -> spine.attempt.offload_runner    <- NO CHANGE NEEDED
            -> offload(live=True, effect_authorization=..., effect_execution=...)

daedalus/spine/attempt.py needs no edit at all: offload_runner already forwards
every extra kwarg to offload verbatim (attempt.py:1113-1127). It also carries
the non-write tasks of a mixed wave, which run_write_wave delegates back to
scheduler.dispatch -- re-keyed, because that call passes a COMPACTED task list
and dispatch derives each execution from the position it sees.

(B) THE GOVERNANCE-HEAD CHECK (HERACLES-SPEND, finding F8). `_governance_verdict`
took `daedalus.core.get_governance`'s `promotion_allowed` and ignored its
`head`, so a discrimination verdict measured at an OLDER HEAD of this same
checkout still unlocked promotion for code the gate had never seen. The hunk
adds `_same_revision`/`_wave_source_revision`, narrows an allow to a hold when
the verdict's revision is not this wave's revision, and passes the primary
checkout's HEAD at the one call site in `run_write_wave`. Narrowing only: a
mismatch (or an unreadable HEAD) can lock promotion, never unlock it, and the
new parameter defaults to None, which is byte-identical to today's behaviour
for any other caller.

The same check now also runs one level up, in the loop driver:
daedalus/loop.py compares `gov_head` against `source_revision` and records
"GOVERNANCE IS ABOUT ANOTHER REVISION" in the report. That one is LANDED. This
hunk is the sealed-path half, so a write wave started by anything other than
LoopDriver is held by the same rule.

WHY IT IS NOT APPLIED HERE. daedalus/kairos/gated_writes.py is in both lanes'
do-not-edit set, and its body is the sealed strangler resource
_gated_writes_legacy.py.src, pinned by git blob sha1 inside gated_writes.py.

